<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24043" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">insŭlāris</span></b> , e,
			adj.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>belonging to an
			island</i>, <i>insular</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">insulari poena multavit,</span>”
				i. e. <i>punished him with banishment to an island</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 15, 7, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">solitudo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 14, 5, 3</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">24, 2, 9 al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-sŭlāres</span></b> , m.
			plur., <i>keepers of a temple</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Just.
				32, 2, 2</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
